.TITLE "wc"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Counts the number of __lines__, __words__, and __bytes__ in a file or piped input. It is a simple but effective tool for analyzing the size and complexity of text data.

.DIV "TLDR"
**wc file**
Displays the count of lines, words, and bytes for a specific file.
> __file__ the target file

**wc -l file**
Displays only the total number of lines in a file.
> __-l__ line count flag | __file__ the target file

**wc -w file**
Displays only the total number of words in a file.
> __-w__ word count flag | __file__ the target file

**wc -c file**
Displays only the total number of bytes (size) of a file.
> __-c__ byte count flag | __file__ the target file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __wc -l__ is a popular way to count the number of items in a list by piping the output of another command (e.g., __ls | wc -l__). It provides a quick numeric summary without needing to read the entire file.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:du** **cli:ls** **cli:grep**

